  "interpretation": "Single-MIR sessions without a typed/untyped split are plotted as Lambda typed. Results5-8 are partial tests and are omitted from the axis. The C2MIR series begins at Result18 because Results2-4 use Lambda scripts through the C2MIR transpiler, while Result18 onward reports native C benchmark ports. Python is reported in Results3-4; Go is reported in Result18. Node.js is the 1.0x reference line. Results39-40 are omitted because they were measured against Node.js v24.7.0 instead of v22.13.0 and are not comparable. Result41 onward covers 63 rows (four text rows added); Result45 omits C2MIR; Result47 omits QuickJS.",
  "title": "Lambda Benchmark History",
  "description": "Line chart of benchmark-session geometric means relative to Node.js from Result1 through Result47, omitting partial Results5 through Result8 and the Node.js v24 Results39-40 from the x-axis; session creation months are shown above the plot. The vertical axis is logarithmic from 0.1x to 100x. Values below 1x are faster than Node.js. Single-MIR sessions before Result16 are assigned to the Lambda typed series, and missing common-engine measurements are gaps.",
